Assume <a href="#num:approximation" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="num:approximation">[num:approximation]</a>, and let $H$ be a very ample Cartier divisor on $Y$. Fix a projective resolution $\pi:\widehat Y\to Y$ which is an isomorphism over the smooth locus. There are a smooth complete intersection surface $S\subset Y$, cut out by $n-2$ members of $|H|$, and a Cartier divisor $P$ on $\widehat Y$ with the following properties. Identify $S$ with its inverse image in $\widehat Y$. Then $L|_S$ is nef, so $$\label{num:nonnegative-square}
L^2\cdot H^{n-2}\geq 0.$$ If $dL$ is Cartier, then for every positive integer $m$ divisible by $d$ the restriction map $$\label{num:restriction-surjective}
H^0(\widehat Y,m\pi^*L+P)
\longrightarrow H^0(S,mL|_S+P|_S)$$ is surjective. In particular, as $m\to\infty$ through multiples of this one fixed integer $d$, $$\label{num:quadratic-growth}
h^0(\widehat Y,m\pi^*L+P)
\geq \frac{m^2}{2}\,L^2\cdot H^{n-2}+O(m),$$ where the error term depends only on the fixed surface and its divisors.

Let $V$ be a smooth projective complex variety, let $\Gamma\subset V$ be an integral curve, and let $\iota:N\to V$ be the map from its normalization. For a section $s$, write $\operatorname{ord}_z(s)$ for its order in the regular local ring of $V$ at $z$. There is a positive constant $g$, depending only on this map, such that for every line bundle $\mathcal D$ on $V$, every nonzero section $s\in H^0(V,\mathcal D)$, and every closed point $z\in\Gamma$, $$\label{num:jet-bound}
\operatorname{ord}_z(s)\geq
-\frac{\deg_N\iota^*\mathcal D}{g}.$$

If a punctured-cone point has stabilizer order $m$, then for every rational $\alpha>0$, $$\label{eq:jet-volume}
V\le
(r+3\alpha)^4\,\frac h{(1+\alpha(mh)^{1/3})^3}.$$

For all integral gradings sufficiently close to the minimizing ray in Proposition <a href="#prop:cone" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:cone">3</a>, every stabilizer order on $C\setminus\{o\}$ satisfies $$\label{eq:stabilizer}
m<\frac r{5/2}.$$ Consequently $$\label{eq:discrepancy-three}
A_C(F)\ge3$$ for every primitive prime divisor $F$ centered at $o$.
